   "s": "TMCV",
   "n": "Tata Motors Limited",
   "cat": "Acquisition",
   "when": "2026-11-26 20:29",
   "sent": "positive",
   "txt": "**1. Most Important Fact**  \nTata Motors Limited\u2019s (formerly TML Commercial Vehicles Limited) shareholding in Automobile Corporation of Goa Limited (ACGL) has passively increased from 48.98% to 50.17% following ACGL's buyback and extinguishment of 1,44,639 equity shares. Consequently, ACGL has transitioned from an associate company to a majority-owned subsidiary and will be fully consolidated.\n\n---\n\n**2. Key Numbers Exactly as Stated**  \n* **Shareholding Change:** Increased by 1.19% (from 48.98% to 50.17%).  \n* **New Shares Acquired / Consideration:** Zero / Not Applicable (passive increase).  \n* **Shares Extinguished by ACGL:** 1,44,639 equity shares.  \n* **ACGL Authorized Share Capital (FY26):** \u20b925,00,00,000  \n* **ACGL Revenue from Operations (last 3 years):**  \n  * **FY25-26:** \u20b9933.65 crore (\u20b9933,65,49,000)  \n  * **FY24-25:** \u20b9660.77 crore  \n  * **FY23-24:** \u20b9584.34 crore  \n*(Note: EBITDA, PAT, and profit margins are not disclosed in the document).*\n\n---\n\n**3. Management Guidance / Forward Statements**  \nNo forward-looking guidance was given, other than stating that *\"ACGL will be consolidated as a subsidiary of the Company\"* and that ACGL's business is aligned with the automotive sector in which the Company operates.\n\n---\n\n**4. What a Shareholder Should Watch or Act On**  \n* **Watch:** The upcoming consolidation of ACGL\u2019s full revenue and balance sheet into Tata Motors\u2019 financial results.  \n* **Action:** None required; the change occurred passively via ACGL's buyback without any capital outlay by Tata Motors.\n\n---\n\n**5. One-Line Net Read**  \n**Neutral to mildly positive:** Tata Motors gains majority control and consolidation of a growing supplier/bus-body manufacturer without incurring any cash expenditure."
  },
