  {
   "s": "LGEINDIA",
   "n": "LG Electronics India Limited",
   "cat": "Updates",
   "when": "2026-11-25 15:15",
   "sent": "negative",
   "txt": "**1. Single Most Important Fact**\nPromoter LG Electronics Inc. intends to sell up to a 2% stake (up to 13,575,447 equity shares) of LG Electronics India Limited in the open market to comply with Minimum Public Shareholding (MPS) requirements, reducing its shareholding from 85.00% to 83.00%.\n\n---\n\n**2. Key Numbers Exactly as Stated**\n*(Note: This is a shareholding/compliance filing, not a financial results filing; no revenue or earnings figures are stated).*\n* **Shares to be divested:** Up to 13,575,447 Equity Shares (Face value \u20b910 each)\n* **Stake to be divested:** Up to 2.00% of total issued and paid-up Equity Share capital\n* **Current Promoter Holding (as on Nov 25, 2026):** 85.00%\n* **Post-Sale Promoter Holding:** 83.00%\n\n---\n\n**3. Management Guidance, Outlook, or Forward Statements**\n* **Completion Timeline:** The divestment process will be completed by **December 31, 2026**, executed in single or multiple tranches.\n* **Undertaking:** The promoter, LG Electronics Inc., has undertaken that neither it nor any entity in the promoter group will purchase any equity shares in the open market on the dates when sales are executed.\n\n---\n\n**4. What a Shareholder Should Watch or Act On**\n* **Supply Overhang:** Potential near-term price pressure from the sale of up to ~13.58 million shares directly into the open market ahead of December 31, 2026.\n* **Future Dilution:** Since promoter holding will still remain at 83.00% post-sale, watch for further divestments required to reach the mandatory 25% public float (75% promoter ceiling) under SEBI MPS rules.\n\n---\n\n**5. One-Line Net Read**\n**Neutral to slightly negative near-term** due to open-market secondary supply overhang, though it is a routine regulatory compliance step."
  },
