   "txt": "### 1. Most Important Fact\nLarsen & Toubro's Renewables business and L&T Electronic Products & Systems (LTEPS) have jointly secured a \"Significant\" order to develop a 300 MW / 900 MWh Battery Energy Storage System (BESS) at Khavda, Gujarat.\n\n### 2. Key Numbers Exactly as Stated\n* **Order Value Classification:** \"Significant\" (defined by L&T as **\u20b91,000 crore to \u20b92,500 crore**).\n* **Project Specifications:**\n  * Power capacity: **300 MW**\n  * Energy storage capacity: **900 MWh** (3-hour BESS)\n* *(Note: Financial metrics such as revenue, EBITDA, margins, or PAT are not present in this contract-win filing.)*\n\n### 3. Forward Statement / Outlook\n* The project will use **liquid-cooling technology** to deliver higher power density, enhanced safety, and longer operating life.\n* The facility will store surplus renewable energy during high generation periods and release it during peak demand to maximize clean energy utilization, improve grid flexibility, and strengthen India's power network.\n\n### 4. What a Shareholder Should Watch or Act On\n* Monitor execution timelines and margins in L&T's expanding green energy / BESS portfolio, which is becoming a core growth driver within its EPC and high-tech offerings.\n* Watch for subsequent updates on client identity and commercial terms.\n\n### 5. Net Read\n**Positive**: Strengthens L&T's order book and enhances its technological track record in India's fast-growing utility-scale energy storage market."
